  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 250 AM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nMonday and Tuesday...As the above mentioned cool core upper low \npropagates acrs MN and IA, it should continue the mostly cloudy and \nlight showery regime for the local area into portions of Tue. \nHighs in the 60s with lows in the 50s. If some clearing occurs \nTue night, currently fcst thicknesses support lows in the 40s. \nIf sfc winds trend light the same night, will have to keep fog \nin mind.\n\nWednesday through Saturday...Quick look at the longer range suggests \nkind of a messy and partially blocked upper air pattern, with \nenough ridging close by or overhead to keep the area mainly dry \nWed into Thu, before an undercutting wave battles the ridging to\nbring the next main chance of rain/showers by Friday into \nFriday night. Temps look seasonable for the end of the week.",
